.TH FL-PAINT 1 "November 2026" "fldesktop 0.1.4" "fldesktop"
.SH NAME
fl-paint \- a simple drawing program
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfl-paint\fR [\fIPICTURE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Draws on pictures: a soft round brush (B), an eraser (E), lines (L),
rectangles (R) and ellipses (O), outlined or filled (Shift: squares and
circles), a fill (F), text (T), a rectangular selection (S) with copy, cut,
paste and crop, and a colour picker (I). [ and ] change the size; Ctrl and
the mouse wheel zoom. Layers can be added, hidden (double-click), moved,
merged and made see-through. Undo and redo go back 25 steps. The picture
can be resized, its canvas enlarged, rotated and flipped.
.PP
PNG, JPEG, BMP and GIF pictures open; pictures are saved as PNG (the layers
merged). Copying also puts the selection on the clipboard as a PNG
(\fBwl-copy\fR).
.SH PEN PRESSURE
\fBView > Pen Pressure\fR (\fBPenPressure=true\fR in \fB[Paint]\fR of
\fI~/.config/fldesktop/paint.ini\fR) makes the brush and the eraser follow how hard a tablet's pen
presses: a fifth of the size at the lightest touch, all of it pressed hard. It uses the Wayland
tablet protocol, from the next start; the compositor then gives the pen to fl-paint as a pen rather
than as a mouse. Off by default.
.SH OPENRASTER
Pictures with layers can be saved as OpenRaster (\fI.ora\fR), the layered format MyPaint,
Krita and GIMP read and write: every layer is kept with its name, opacity and visibility, and
the file also holds the merged picture and a thumbnail. Save As offers it when the picture
has more than one layer; PNG merges the layers. OpenRaster files from other programs open
with their layers (offsets are kept, groups are flattened into the layer list).
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBfl-view\fR(1), \fBfl-snip\fR(1)
